    "According to you, how can LLMs be used to innovate math learning in schools and universities?": "LLMs can make math less scary. They can explain concepts in simple words, like how I'd explain baking. They can give practice problems tailored to your level. They could connect math to real life, like chemistry or cooking. If used right, they help confidence. But they shouldn't replace human teachers. Just a tool, not the whole meal."
